<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Cheesecake</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/recipes.css">

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Jacques+Francois&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Crimson+Text:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,400;1,600;1,700&family=Jacques+Francois&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

</head>
<body>
    <h1>Cheesecake</h1>
    <p>This is a delicious cheesecake recipe.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Ingredients:
            <ul>
                <li>200g digestive biscuits</li>
                <li>100g butter, melted</li>
                <li>600g cream cheese</li>
                <li>200g sugar</li>
                <li>200ml sour cream</li>
                <li>3 eggs</li>
                <li>1 tsp vanilla extract</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <br>
        <li>Instructions:
            <ol>
                <li>Preheat the oven to 160°C (320°F).</li>
                <li>Crush the biscuits and mix with melted butter. Press into the base of a springform pan.</li>
                <li>In a large bowl, beat the cream cheese and sugar until smooth.</li>
                <li>Add sour cream, eggs, and vanilla extract. Mix until well combined.</li>
                <li>Pour the mixture over the biscuit base.</li>
                <li>Bake for 50-60 minutes or until the center is set.</li>
                <li>Let it cool and refrigerate for at least 4 hours before serving.</li>
            </ol>
        </li>
    </ul>
</body>
</html>